{
  "title": "Common-source amplifier",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "SKY130 NFET common-source: gm·RD inverting gain (nfet_01v8, W = 10 µm, VDD = 1.8 V, RD = 12 kΩ)",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -173,
        "title": "Common-source amplifier — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A real SKY130 nfet_01v8 (MN, W = 10 um, L = 0.15 um) in",
          "common-source: VDD = 1.8 V feeds the drain through load",
          "resistor RD = 12 kohm, which sets the DC operating point.",
          "The gate is biased at VB = 0.72 V (drain near mid-rail)",
          "with a small 20 mV, 10 MHz sine VIN riding on top. In",
          "saturation the small-signal gain is -gm*RD (~8x here),",
          "so probe vout at the drain is an inverted, amplified",
          "copy of probe vin. Source and",
          "bulk are grounded (GS, GBK); CL is the output load.",
          "",
          "Set RD.R = 24000 and re-run to roughly double the gain",
          "(and watch the DC drain point drop toward the rail)."
        ]
      }
    ],
